# Wave W17-U (Route 203): cart post — a cart-track marker post where the stone thickens: a heavy post bound with one dark iron band, the mark the cart crews repaint each spring where their track leaves the road for the mine country (design: cart tracks crossing the thinning grass east). On coal turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 202’s pale-banded city posts by the iron band: the city announces, the mine country just marks the turn.
